                        "tags": [
                            "future"
                        ],
                        "form": "буду/будешь… противополага́ть"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9f72ce2c-01a6-3b43-9d87-8611fcb4119d",
                        "entry_id": "387cc8fa-827a-309c-ad7d-2aaf49340813",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. сравнивать, сопоставлять с кем-либо, чем-либо, указывая несходность признаков одного и другого, давать рядом что-либо несходное по каким-либо признакам"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b3145c5-65cb-4245-a79d-e3cfe0950f9b",
                                "sense_id": "9f72ce2c-01a6-3b43-9d87-8611fcb4119d",
                                "text": "Во-первых, ценность человечности не следует совсем противополагать божественному превосходству."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3cc61487-bc3d-3af9-a133-6aef67f2f6e7",
                        "entry_id": "387cc8fa-827a-309c-ad7d-2aaf49340813",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. направлять, выставлять, обращая против кого-либо, чего-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "07bfcaf1-712b-427c-842f-5dbeafb178b9",
                                "sense_id": "3cc61487-bc3d-3af9-a133-6aef67f2f6e7",
                                "text": "Неверно поймут меня те, которые решат, что я вселенскую идею противополагаю родине."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cc789bc7-8f0c-491c-8b56-120b725e9121",
                        "source_entry_id": "387cc8fa-827a-309c-ad7d-2aaf49340813",
                        "source_sense_description": "сопоставлять с кем-либо, чем-либо, указывая несходность признаков",
                        "target_lang_word": "contrast",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "contrast",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6dbd284-0418-3778-a0bc-86dcc8998a2d",
                                        "entry_id": "205ff059-6074-32ff-9a0a-6e45ba8318c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A difference in lightness, brightness or hue between two colours that makes them more or less distinguishable.",
                                            "The degree of this difference."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0156f42f-7bbe-4840-bbab-5b0f149e0e84",
                                                "sense_id": "a6dbd284-0418-3778-a0bc-86dcc8998a2d",
                                                "text": "The red and the orange don't have much contrast between them — I can hardly tell them apart."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2b9d67d-a296-3a1a-906c-d518065c5c78",
                                        "entry_id": "205ff059-6074-32ff-9a0a-6e45ba8318c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A difference in lightness, brightness or hue between two colours that makes them more or less distinguishable.",
                                            "A control on a television, etc, that adjusts the amount of contrast in the images being displayed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3881c1ba-8cef-4854-b5e8-f4fe6182cb59",
                                                "sense_id": "d2b9d67d-a296-3a1a-906c-d518065c5c78",
                                                "text": "Ohh, you can't fool me. This thing's top of the line! It's got two contrast knobs!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "383e7ff9-9e94-3d93-bd48-ffacb2e8c74d",
                                        "entry_id": "205ff059-6074-32ff-9a0a-6e45ba8318c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A difference between two objects, people or concepts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "385f9c77-df98-4f52-8b77-47b219c98a0e",
                                                "sense_id": "383e7ff9-9e94-3d93-bd48-ffacb2e8c74d",
                                                "text": "Israel is a country of many contrasts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87853bf7-8add-4ef0-a6fa-0631c07a41fc",
                                                "sense_id": "383e7ff9-9e94-3d93-bd48-ffacb2e8c74d",
                                                "text": "The colonel and his sponsor made a queer contrast: Greystone [the sponsor] long and stringy, with a face that seemed as if a cold wind was eternally playing on it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "555725e7-40bd-4229-96dc-39535e8e1c89",
                                                "sense_id": "383e7ff9-9e94-3d93-bd48-ffacb2e8c74d",
                                                "text": "... there is no quality in this world that is not what it is merely by contrast."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac3bd35f-c2e9-3d8a-b4ce-1eedb6106ca8",
                                        "entry_id": "205ff059-6074-32ff-9a0a-6e45ba8318c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that is opposite of or strikingly different from something else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b7c5313-6b04-4f38-9c7d-ea8f824b14af",
                                                "sense_id": "ac3bd35f-c2e9-3d8a-b4ce-1eedb6106ca8",
                                                "text": "Why this denunciation of idolatry at this point? And why are Shabbat and the sanctuary mentioned as contrasts to idol worship?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f56ec925-e0dd-3296-b94c-1e812e71a539",
                                        "entry_id": "205ff059-6074-32ff-9a0a-6e45ba8318c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Antithesis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rhetoric",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbda90a0-c601-3a52-a4b6-faa60207cb2a",
                                        "entry_id": "205ff059-6074-32ff-9a0a-6e45ba8318c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Contrast medium"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "contrast",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69ae0b5b-cfdc-3b86-b5e7-638bb9314180",
                                        "entry_id": "adc5e023-ea69-3d40-a551-affe8debe78a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To set in opposition in order to show the difference or differences between; to counterpoint."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3103475-87c5-3b90-b7e9-279f470273e2",
                                        "entry_id": "adc5e023-ea69-3d40-a551-affe8debe78a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To form a contrast."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d410901-a30a-4452-819f-1ca773dd6f44",
                                                "sense_id": "f3103475-87c5-3b90-b7e9-279f470273e2",
                                                "text": "Foreground and background strongly contrast."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c2c5e44-97a5-4c3d-a290-58502b8daa2a",
                                                "sense_id": "f3103475-87c5-3b90-b7e9-279f470273e2",
                                                "text": "The color of her dress contrasts very nicely with the black scarf around her neck."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73926711-4b90-4952-b2a8-4c96a351fb81",
                                                "sense_id": "f3103475-87c5-3b90-b7e9-279f470273e2",
                                                "text": "The joints which divide the sandstone contrast finely with the divisional planes which separate the basalt into pillars."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "07c1bc58-3690-407c-b93c-e76f5d5f05db",
                        "source_entry_id": "387cc8fa-827a-309c-ad7d-2aaf49340813",
                        "source_sense_description": "сопоставлять с кем-либо, чем-либо, указывая несходность признаков",
                        "target_lang_word": "set off",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "set off",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "137c5a4c-40c7-3872-af23-33f87ffea36a",
                                        "entry_id": "b20dd828-5904-3319-bd3a-4ffc6db00b63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To leave; to set out; to begin a journey or trip."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22458f37-dc6c-4c9f-9bb5-9aaa32cfc193",
                                                "sense_id": "137c5a4c-40c7-3872-af23-33f87ffea36a",
                                                "text": "He set off in search of better opportunities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9aa7c6b2-f498-41d2-b341-b0a0940d65b6",
                                                "sense_id": "137c5a4c-40c7-3872-af23-33f87ffea36a",
                                                "text": "Considerable excitement was caused on the L.M.S.R. Aberdeen line out of Perth recently when a shunting engine in Perth North goods yard, whose driver and fireman were absent, was accidentally set in motion by a shunter and set off unattended on to the main line."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ccf5c5f-a509-4b94-9116-6b003ffc4115",
                                                "sense_id": "137c5a4c-40c7-3872-af23-33f87ffea36a",
                                                "text": "The train is booked to stop at Jiza for only three minutes, but more often than not twenty minutes or more are spent on shunting before it sets off again on what must be one of the most dreary journeys in the world."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91f0a622-cfb7-397f-8c35-e6b7f651fc74",
                                        "entry_id": "b20dd828-5904-3319-bd3a-4ffc6db00b63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To begin; to cause; to initiate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bee4be3-61a0-4a7b-b4b8-513a0409028f",
                                                "sense_id": "91f0a622-cfb7-397f-8c35-e6b7f651fc74",
                                                "text": "I had no idea that one simple comment would set off such a huge argument."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f745647-9643-3afc-9baf-a59d7093b9cd",
                                        "entry_id": "b20dd828-5904-3319-bd3a-4ffc6db00b63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause to explode, let off."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "744a9222-da7d-4dd3-a34c-af8ce90efb4a",
                                                "sense_id": "0f745647-9643-3afc-9baf-a59d7093b9cd",
                                                "text": "What a tragedy, that someone would set off a bomb in a crowded place."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a42236e4-cdf5-4601-b255-f7f8a1ee889c",
                                                "sense_id": "0f745647-9643-3afc-9baf-a59d7093b9cd",
                                                "text": "Wrex: There are acid tanks rigged up on that thing. Set them off. Millions of my ancestors died to put these things down. Don't let them come back."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d593289f-9c36-3dbf-9316-fe1938d2033b",
                                        "entry_id": "b20dd828-5904-3319-bd3a-4ffc6db00b63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put into an angry mood; to start (a person) ranting or sulking, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0680def4-aaa8-4d6b-8303-a0c3d506ea86",
                                                "sense_id": "d593289f-9c36-3dbf-9316-fe1938d2033b",
                                                "text": "Don't set him off or he won't shut up all day."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63cc5575-dbad-3669-a8f8-8b07aa08e5b8",
                                        "entry_id": "b20dd828-5904-3319-bd3a-4ffc6db00b63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To enhance by emphasizing differences."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "573a22db-7dad-453b-a16c-57e51dcdc8ba",
                                                "sense_id": "63cc5575-dbad-3669-a8f8-8b07aa08e5b8",
                                                "text": "Her plain white dress was set off by a bright red stole."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "067e33d3-eed1-493b-a0c0-41d8e6accec5",
                                                "sense_id": "63cc5575-dbad-3669-a8f8-8b07aa08e5b8",
                                                "text": "And then one afternoon in the hinder end of April came young Heriotside riding to the Skerburnfoot. His arm was healed, he had got him a fine new suit of green, and his horse was a mettle beast that well set off his figure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "996090e9-20f2-3f82-aaea-42166f56d157",
                                        "entry_id": "b20dd828-5904-3319-bd3a-4ffc6db00b63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To offset, to compensate for: to reduce the effect of, by having a contrary effect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc541a51-5fe5-4e4b-ab4c-2fd1b5568b3d",
                                                "sense_id": "996090e9-20f2-3f82-aaea-42166f56d157",
                                                "text": "My taxes did not increase because the amount of my raise was set off by my losses in the stock market."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68346f30-69a1-4ec7-9c5d-dac208cabeca",
                                                "sense_id": "996090e9-20f2-3f82-aaea-42166f56d157",
                                                "text": "When a woman had made such a mistake, there was only one way to repair it,—to accept it. One folly was enough, especially it was to last for ever; a second one would not much set it off."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd125fc1-1144-3d76-be17-7183807aebca",
